sification":"Photograph","accessionNumber":"2025.96.2","description":""},{"id":"232172","title":"Portrait of a Couple","artist":"Augustus Washington","image":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/07a21e2d-0b68-488a-b418-59edf96015cd/full/!843,843/0/default.jpg","fullRes":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/07a21e2d-0b68-488a-b418-59edf96015cd/full/max/0/default.jpg","imageWidth":8707,"imageHeight":10037,"rights":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks/232172","date":"c. 1850","medium":"daguerreotype","dimensions":"image (visible): 7 × 5.5 cm (2 3/4 × 2 3/16 in.)\r\nmat: 8.2 × 7 cm (3 1/4 × 2 3/4 in.)\r\ncase (closed): 9.1 × 8.2 × 1.8 cm (3 9/16 × 3 1/4 × 11/16 in.)","creditLine":"Ross J. Kelbaugh Collection, Pepita Milmore Memorial Fund","classification":"Photograph","accessionNumber":"2025.72.10","description":"This grayscale photograph is a portrait of two people, visible from the knees up. They both have pale skin and dark hair. A man is seated on the left, facing forward. He has pale skin and short, dark hair styled into a curl on top of his head. He is wearing a dark suit with a white shirt and a black collar. A woman is seated on the right. Her hair is parted in the middle and styled into bunches above her ears. She is wearing a dark dress with a checkered pattern around the collar and white cuffs. She holds a small book in her hands. The backdrop is plain and dark. The photograph is enclosed in a gold frame with some dark specks and discolorations. Around that frame is a dark wooden frame with some red trim."},{"id":"232364","title":"Portrait of Berthe Morisot","artist":"Marcellin-Gilbert Desboutin","image":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/057cd462-64fd-4584-be5a-15ed341b0152/full/!843,843/0/default.jpg","fullRes":"https://api.nga.gov/iiif/057cd462-64fd-4584-be5a-15ed341b0152/full/max/0/default.jpg","imageWidth":8519,"imageHeight":12191,"rights":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://www.nga.gov/artworks/232364","date":"c. 1876","medium":"drypoint on wove paper","dimensions":"plate: 26.5 × 1